":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T21:46:26-08:00","id":1049142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1049141#post1049141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I finished reading it. It was really good! The setting, the characters, and the conflict were really well designed. The amnesia of the Arisen was front and center in a really great way. I'm a big fan of the new merits, although the utterances...I need to think about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind teasing some of those Merits?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T22:07:32-08:00","id":1049143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1049142#post1049142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind teasing some of those Merits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure! The new merits expand and augment the Tomb merit from the core. Now, all such Lifeweb-manipulating buildings are known as Neithian Architecture. When you build one, it gets one free Purpose. <br /> <br /> This can be<br /> <br /> Tomb!<br /> Fortress<br /> Guildhall<br /> Palace<br /> Temple<br /> Oasis (naturally occurring lifeweb)<br /> <br /> Each one provides a combination of allowed Aspects, which can be purchased with merit dots:<br /> <br /> Djed (Stave off descent)<br /> Geometry (recharge pillars)<br /> Mirage (refreshes memory)<br /> Peril<br /> Tekhen (Obelisks that suppress pillars)<br /> <br /> There are also new Drawbacks and Endowments. My favorite is Alien Attractor, which turns your tomb into a place of power (Wyrms Nest, Haunt, Hallow, Locus, that kinda thing.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T22:30:07-08:00","id":1049147,"title":"","content":"Just woke up after a terrible work day so just diving into the new Merit set up and the Utterances so far!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T22:32:00-08:00","id":1049148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1049143#post1049143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure! The new merits expand and augment the Tomb merit from the core. Now, all such Lifeweb-manipulating buildings are known as Neithian Architecture. When you build one, it gets one free Purpose. <br /> <br /> This can be<br /> <br /> Tomb!<br /> Fortress<br /> Guildhall<br /> Palace<br /> Temple<br /> Oasis (naturally occurring lifeweb)<br /> <br /> Each one provides a combination of allowed Aspects, which can be purchased with merit dots:<br /> <br /> Djed (Stave off descent)<br /> Geometry (recharge pillars)<br /> Mirage (refreshes memory)<br /> Peril<br /> Tekhen (Obelisks that suppress pillars)<br /> <br /> There are also new Drawbacks and Endowments. My favorite is Alien Attractor, which turns your tomb into a place of power (Wyrms Nest, Haunt, Hallow, Locus, that kinda thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That is all AWESOME! Thanks for sharing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-14T22:34:38-08:00","id":1049149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1049143#post1049143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alien Attractor</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely had a second there where I wondered if my alien ghosts practicing the Ancestry of Forgotten Stars Utterance from the Old Gods campaign had become canon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T16:20:59-08:00","id":1049554,"title":"","content":"Man, I swear the Fountains of Ma' at are almost 100% how I stated up the Lazarus Pits. It makes sense, I tied them to the fountain of youth, too. I love the in-story explanation/mystery regarding their origins, too. Scary implications that once again make me think the shaniatu were endgame level mummies of a previous rite of return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T18:18:16-08:00","id":1049630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1049554#post1049554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, I swear the Fountains of Ma' at are almost 100% how I stated up the Lazarus Pits. It makes sense, I tied them to the fountain of youth, too. I love the in-story explanation/mystery regarding their origins, too. Scary implications that once again make me think the shaniatu were endgame level mummies of a previous rite of return.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;oh look, sekham magic that predates the Nameless Empire.&quot; I love a good mystery.<br /> <br /> I also love the Iron Bull and it's cult of Moloch. The real question is if the First Meret was sent away to protect them from it, or if it had them sent away to protect itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T19:08:26-08:00","id":1049647,"title":"","content":"I haven't dived too deeply into it, but Shan'iatu being previous mummies or older Sekhem magic reminds me of the bit in Sothis Ascends that proposes the Nameless Empire and Rite of Return may have just been the latest in a long cycle of related events","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:48:26-08:00","id":1050037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1049143#post1049143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure! The new merits expand and augment the Tomb merit from the core. Now, all such Lifeweb-manipulating buildings are known as Neithian Architecture. When you build one, it gets one free Purpose. <br /> <br /> This can be<br /> <br /> Tomb!<br /> Fortress<br /> Guildhall<br /> Palace<br /> Temple<br /> Oasis (naturally occurring lifeweb)<br /> <br /> Each one provides a combination of allowed Aspects, which can be purchased with merit dots:<br /> <br /> Djed (Stave off descent)<br /> Geometry (recharge pillars)<br /> Mirage (refreshes memory)<br /> Peril<br /> Tekhen (Obelisks that suppress pillars)<br /> <br /> There are also new Drawbacks and Endowments. My favorite is Alien Attractor, which turns your tomb into a place of power (Wyrms Nest, Haunt, Hallow, Locus, that kinda thing.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So we're already familiar with Tomb and Temple, but what do Fortresses, Guild Halls, and Palaces do? Why do Oases exist? How do Mirages, Djed and Tekhn function?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:16:01-08:00","id":1050054,"title":"","content":"I'm profoundly cutious about Oasis, Tekhen, and Mirage.<br /> <br /> Think any of this could make it into an eventual 2e core?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T16:51:00-08:00","id":1050151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1050054#post1050054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm profoundly cutious about Oasis, Tekhen, and Mirage.<br /> <br /> Think any of this could make it into an eventual 2e core?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given how we've gotten awesome little goodies spread throughout the line I would not be surprised. Though I suppose it would depend on how different things are changed up mechanically in a 2e iteration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T17:43:11-08:00","id":1050178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1050037#post1050037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So we're already familiar with Tomb and Temple, but what do Fortresses, Guild Halls, and Palaces do? Why do Oases exist? How do Mirages, Djed and Tekhn function?</div> </div> </div> </div>So some of these purposes have innate benefits as well as allowing the purchase of a set of Aspects. <br /> <br /> Fortresses add to the stats of your cultists that have been called into combat, and troop losses don't cause Reach/Grasp ratings to decay.<br /> Guildhalls add to guild status when an Arisen claims it with a relic (all of these structures can be claimed by centering one's relic in the lifeweb).<br /> Oases...have no innate properties. I don't really get the point of Oases since they are just naturally occurring lifewebs. Maybe they're just designed for Storytellers to create and players to acquire.<br /> Palaces let Arisen recharge willpower by directing their Cults and it makes it easier to substitute the cult rating for another social merit. <br /> Temples are places of worship and they boost reach and grasp due to the fanaticism they inspire. You also sacrifice relics to duat here as in a tomb.<br /> Tombs work the way they do in Mummy: the Curse Core. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:12:11-08:00","id":1050200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1050178#post1050178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So some of these purposes have innate benefits as well as allowing the purchase of a set of Aspects. <br /> <br /> Fortresses add to the stats of your cultists that have been called into combat, and troop losses don't cause Reach/Grasp ratings to decay.<br /> Guildhalls add to guild status when an Arisen claims it with a relic (all of these structures can be claimed by centering one's relic in the lifeweb).<br /> Oases...have no innate properties. I don't really get the point of Oases since they are just naturally occurring lifewebs. Maybe they're just designed for Storytellers to create and players to acquire.<br /> Palaces let Arisen recharge willpower by directing their Cults and it makes it easier to substitute the cult rating for another social merit. <br /> Temples are places of worship and they boost reach and grasp due to the fanaticism they inspire. You also sacrifice relics to duat here as in a tomb.<br /> Tombs work the way they do in Mummy: the Curse Core. </div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Althouch I swear the Curse of the Mummy refers to the cursing all of the non-backers waiting for this book. Super interesting snippets though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5