-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1049630#post1049630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;oh look, sekham magic that predates the Nameless Empire.&quot; I love a good mystery.<br /> <br /> I also love the Iron Bull and it's cult of Moloch. The real question is if the First Meret was sent away to protect them from it, or if it had them sent away to protect itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>wait.. Cult of Moloch?<br /> <br /> *looks at a huge amount of homebrew, writings and an whole Chronicle built around Moloch*<br /> <br /> I <i>need</i> that book","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T06:18:36-08:00","id":1055207,"title":"","content":"Want some irony? <br /> <br /> I DID back the Mummy kickstarter, but it turns out I'm not so in to it as you guys are. <br /> <br /> The Mummies feel more NPCish then suitable for player characters, and Mummies feel almost unusable for crossovers with other splats except as NPCs. <br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, the setting and horror are outstanding, but I just don't like the mechanics, especially of the descent.<br /> <br /> And it should have used 2e mechanics, I understand why it doesn't, but I have no desire to play 1e. <br /> <br /> <br /> Rio was a lot of fun to read, but I'd never use it, except to add some extra antagonists to a possible future Rio 2e Giest game. <br /> <br /> Still I suppose I should update my copy of the Mummy core to the finalized version soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 02-26-2017, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T06:39:19-08:00","id":1055211,"title":"","content":"I never understand when people say it's not crossover-friendly. There's a bit more player buy-in, like Promethean, because mummies have many supernatural drives that are near compulsions at times (but most splats do, actually) but I wouldn't interpret that as them being better suited to NPCs.<br /> <br /> I think it's due to the books not really going into the topic, unlike Promethean, Changeling, and Demon's supplements. Of course Hunter and Beast are crossover-friendly, and Mage is, too, as it's their nature to study Mysteries. Despite Changeling's Rite of Spring book I don't think that gameline is good for crossover any more than Mummy, what with a very secluded cosmology. The same might be said for Vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T08:23:51-08:00","id":1055249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1055211#post1055211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never understand when people say it's not crossover-friendly. There's a bit more player buy-in, like Promethean, because mummies have many supernatural drives that are near compulsions at times (but most splats do, actually) but I wouldn't interpret that as them being better suited to NPCs.<br /> <br /> I think it's due to the books not really going into the topic, unlike Promethean, Changeling, and Demon's supplements. Of course Hunter and Beast are crossover-friendly, and Mage is, too, as it's their nature to study Mysteries. Despite Changeling's Rite of Spring book I don't think that gameline is good for crossover any more than Mummy, what with a very secluded cosmology. The same might be said for Vampire</div> </div> </div> </div>110% agree. Mummy is no worse at crossover than vampire. In fact, given that Mummies deal with ghosts, they may actually be more Crossover friendly than Requiem since ghosts have another gamelines in Geist and are featured in all the core rulebooks except Blood &amp; Smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:51:23-08:00","id":1055372,"title":"","content":"I'd rather play Mummy in 1E than any 2E game line <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Most of my players are of the same opinion, they got a massive kick out of playing the game. I'd honestly be surprised at any player who turns their nose up at the idea of being one of the true horrors in the darkness, the kind of creature even the Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, and others are scared of. It says something that probably the easiest way to weave Mummy into crossover is to have the other player character monsters be part of a cult <i>worshipping </i>the Mummy PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:08:57-08:00","id":1055385,"title":"","content":"deleted by user","signature":"","edited":{"userid":747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","user":"Knowbody","date":". 02-26-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T21:31:14-08:00","id":1055531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1055156#post1055156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait.. Cult of Moloch?<br /> <br /> *looks at a huge amount of homebrew, writings and an whole Chronicle built around Moloch*<br /> <br /> I <i>need</i> that book</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. This particular cult of Moloch was centered in Carthage around the second turn or so, but in my headcanon, it had jumped around from Minoan Greece and the Levant before that. In this incarnation, the Cult centers around a relic that turns human sacrifices into Sekhem. And gradually creates a second personality in the minds of mummies that use it. Creating a weird hellfire club like cult, led by split personality mummies and an almost-but-not-quite-self-aware Relic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T21:35:26-08:00","id":1055533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1055531#post1055531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. This particular cult of Moloch was centered in Carthage around the second turn or so, but in my headcanon, it had jumped around from Minoan Greece and the Levant before that. In this incarnation, the Cult centers around a relic that turns human sacrifices into Sekhem. And gradually creates a second personality in the minds of mummies that use it. Creating a weird hellfire club like cult, led by split personality mummies and an almost-but-not-quite-self-aware Relic.</div> </div> </div> </div>......I need it even more","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T01:49:55-08:00","id":1055567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1055531#post1055531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. This particular cult of Moloch was centered in Carthage around the second turn or so, but in my headcanon, it had jumped around from Minoan Greece and the Levant before that. In this incarnation, the Cult centers around a relic that turns human sacrifices into Sekhem. And gradually creates a second personality in the minds of mummies that use it. Creating a weird hellfire club like cult, led by split personality mummies and an almost-but-not-quite-self-aware Relic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the Iron Bull is aware; it just doesn't care. Kind of like a G-M Angel or Infrastructure. It creates the personality to overcome the 'failings' of people who balk at feeding it multiple child sacrifices on a regular basis; as that is the most efficient manner to use it's abilities. Also adds more than just Sekham; the architecture rules mean that it isn't just a buzzword, there are actual mechanics now. Heck, the Relic teaches unique Utterances. The Word cannot be used without the Will.<br /> <br /> I also like the Utterances that they supposedly learned from Spirits. Too bad we won't get DIY Utterance guidlines this edition, but they have opened the door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T03:55:11-08:00","id":1055588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/811476-cursed-necropolis-rio?p=1055211#post1055211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never understand when people say it's not crossover-friendly. There's a bit more player buy-in, like Promethean, because mummies have many supernatural drives that are near compulsions at times (but most splats do, actually) but I wouldn't interpret that as them being better suited to NPCs.<br /> <br /> I think it's due to the books not really going into the topic, unlike Promethean, Changeling, and Demon's supplements. Of course Hunter and Beast are crossover-friendly, and Mage is, too, as it's their nature to study Mysteries. Despite Changeling's Rite of Spring book I don't think that gameline is good for crossover any more than Mummy, what with a very secluded cosmology. The same might be said for Vampire</div> </div> </div> </div> Fluff wise you make a good point, but mechanically Mage and Mummies are so powerful compared to other splats that they cause all kinds of problems. A dev came out and out right admitted Mates, Mummies, and Demons are out right more powerful then the other splats by design. <br /> <br /> When they do the Crossover Chronicles they have their work cut out for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T04:24:34-08:00","id":1055590,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'll give you that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T12:26:53-08:00","id":106